{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"coverage\":[{\"reason\":\"Defines private market assets and direct or indirect exposure routes.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u1.5\"},{\"reason\":\"Defines covered SFC-authorised Funds and separates disclosure from possible classification.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u4.564\"},{\"reason\":\"Describes risks motivating scrutiny, without creating automatic tests.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u7.1028\"},{\"reason\":\"Sets information and distributor expectations, distinct from classification.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u10.1937\"},{\"reason\":\"Disclosure heading.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u11.2466\"},{\"reason\":\"Requires disclosure where exposure may exist; does not itself classify.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u14.2516\"},{\"reason\":\"Exposure extent and access disclosures may inform assessment; examples are not thresholds.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u15.2718\"},{\"reason\":\"Underlying-asset characteristics disclosure may inform discretionary assessment.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u16.2995\"},{\"reason\":\"Risk disclosure remains distinct from classification.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u17.3223\"},{\"reason\":\"Classification heading.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u18.3743\"},{\"reason\":\"Creates the 50% aggregate threshold and separate SFC designation power.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u21.3779\"},{\"reason\":\"Aggregate exposure is a discretionary factor as well.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u22.4078\"},{\"reason\":\"Strategy, composition, liquidity and risk profile are discretionary factors.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u24.4176\"},{\"reason\":\"Asset extent and characteristics, including CLO and SRT details, are discretionary factors.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u26.4290\"},{\"reason\":\"Home-regulator conditions are discretionary factors.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u28.4505\"},{\"reason\":\"Requires holistic case-specific assessment.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u29.4630\"},{\"reason\":\"Classification triggers prevailing complex-product sales requirements and suitability.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u32.4805\"},{\"reason\":\"Target-market and distributor heading.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u33.5086\"},{\"reason\":\"References separate product-approval guidance whose full text is unavailable.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u36.5149\"},{\"reason\":\"Requires target-market matching and distributor knowledge of complex status.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u39.5617\"},{\"reason\":\"Advertising duties do not determine classification.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u42.6275\"},{\"reason\":\"Organisational heading.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u43.6653\"},{\"reason\":\"New funds may receive scrutiny or FASTrack exclusion, distinct from classification.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u46.6668\"},{\"reason\":\"Existing funds must review and act promptly; no grandfathering stated.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u49.6955\"},{\"reason\":\"Identifies clarification route.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u52.7565\"},{\"reason\":\"Identifies issuing division.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u55.7698\"},{\"reason\":\"Identifies issuing regulator.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u56.7736\"},{\"reason\":\"Separate 15% direct-investment limit does not replace the 50% classification threshold.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u58.7778\"},{\"reason\":\"Indirect-exposure examples are non-exhaustive and updateable.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u59.7979\"},{\"reason\":\"Defines BDC exposure route.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u60.8163\"},{\"reason\":\"Defines CLO exposure route.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u61.8338\"},{\"reason\":\"Illustrates TRS and SRT routes without exhaustive measurement rules.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u62.8487\"},{\"reason\":\"Excludes LAFs from this circular and refers to a separate regime.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u63.8691\"},{\"reason\":\"Limits the footnote-7 discretion to exposure below 50%.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u64.8910\"},{\"reason\":\"Identifies external sales rules and FAQs, not fully supplied.\",\"status\":\"INTERPRETED\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u65.9044\"},{\"reason\":\"Dates separate product-approval guidance only.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u66.9304\"},{\"reason\":\"Dates referenced advertising guidance only.\",\"status\":\"CONTEXT\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u67.9509\"}],\"dimensions\":[{\"dimension\":\"scope\",\"explanation\":\"Applies to funds authorised by the SFC for public offering in Hong Kong, excluding listed closed-ended alternative asset funds. Managers, the SFC and distributors have the stated roles; existing funds are covered and new funds may receive separate scrutiny.\",\"source_unit_ids\":[\"d4148dd852cee.u4.564\",\"d4148dd852cee.u39.5617\",\"d4148dd852cee.u46.6668\",\"d4148dd852cee.u49.6955\",\"d4148dd852cee.u63.8691\"],\"status\":\"PROPOSED\"},{\"dimension\":\"definitions\",\"explanation\":\"Private market assets are private credit and private equity. Aggregate exposure combines direct and indirect exposure, with BDCs, CLOs, TRSs and SRTs illustrative and non-exhaustive. Exactly 50% of NAV meets the stated threshold. Look-through, netting, valuation, derivative treatment and actual versus intended or permitted exposure are unspecified.\",\"source_unit_ids\":[\"d4148dd852cee.u1.5\",\"d4148dd852cee.u21.3779\",\"d4148dd852cee.u59.7979\",\"d4148dd852cee.u60.8163\",\"d4148dd852cee.u61.8338\",\"d4148dd852cee.u62.8487\"],\"status\":\"AMBIGUOUS\"},{\"dimension\":\"exceptions\",\"explanation\":\"LAFs are outside this circular, not declared non-complex. Below 50% is not a safe harbour because SFC designation remains possible. The 15% direct-investment limit is separate. No existing-fund, unsolicited-sale or grandfathering exception is stated.\",\"source_unit_ids\":[\"d4148dd852cee.u63.8691\",\"d4148dd852cee.u64.8910\",\"d4148dd852cee.u58.7778\",\"d4148dd852cee.u32.4805\",\"d4148dd852cee.u49.6955\"],\"status\":\"PROPOSED\"},{\"dimension\":\"modality\",\"explanation\":\"At least 50% aggregate exposure mandates complex classification. Below 50%, the SFC may designate after a holistic, non-exhaustive assessment; listed factors do not automatically designate. Disclosure, advertising, review and distributor guidance are separate duties.\",\"source_unit_ids\":[\"d4148dd852cee.u21.3779\",\"d4148dd852cee.u22.4078\",\"d4148dd852cee.u24.4176\",\"d4148dd852cee.u26.4290\",\"d4148dd852cee.u28.4505\",\"d4148dd852cee.u29.4630\",\"d4148dd852cee.u64.8910\"],\"status\":\"PROPOSED\"},{\"dimension\":\"time\",\"explanation\":\"The retained text supplies no commencement date, transition deadline, observation frequency, threshold-duration rule or declassification procedure. Existing managers must update documents as soon as practicable and may consult early. Dates 2014-04-30, 2016-03-04 and April 2013 date referenced guidance, not this classification rule.\",\"source_unit_ids\":[\"d4148dd852cee.u49.6955\",\"d4148dd852cee.u66.9304\",\"d4148dd852cee.u67.9509\"],\"status\":\"AMBIGUOUS\"},{\"dimension\":\"dependencies\",\"explanation\":\"A decision requires authorisation and LAF evidence, a supported exposure calculation and evidence of any operative SFC designation. UT Code 7.3, the LAF circular, sales rules and FAQs, product-approval guidance and advertising guidelines are incomplete here. The three listed missing dependencies have no content or mapping, so their qualifications cannot be inferred.\",\"source_unit_ids\":[\"d4148dd852cee.u58.7778\",\"d4148dd852cee.u63.8691\",\"d4148dd852cee.u65.9044\",\"d4148dd852cee.u66.9304\",\"d4148dd852cee.u67.9509\"],\"status\":\"AMBIGUOUS\"}],\"questions\":[\"What evidence establishes SFC authorisation, LAF status, aggregate exposure relative to NAV and any operative SFC designation?\",\"What measurement basis applies to actual, intended or permitted exposure, including look-through, derivatives, netting, valuation and temporary crossings?\",\"What commencement, transition, reassessment and declassification rules arise from the missing materials or SFC clarification?\"],\"readings\":[{\"assumptions\":[\"The result answers only whether a classification ground under this circular is satisfied at the relevant assessment time.\",\"An operative SFC designation requires evidence of an actual case-specific decision; risk factors or absence of a located decision do not resolve it.\",\"Unknown exposure measurement or missing evidence remains unknown rather than false.\",\"The circular's threshold and below-threshold discretionary distinction are retained, while the basis and timing of measurement remain unresolved.\"],\"citations\":[{\"quote\":\"A Fund will be considered as a complex product if its total direct and indirect exposures to private market assets amount to 50% or more of the Fund’s NAV.\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u21.3779\"},{\"quote\":\"On a case-by-case basis, the SFC may also designate a Fund as a complex product, taking into account factors including, without limitation:\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u21.3779\"},{\"quote\":\"In cases where the Fund’s aggregate direct and indirect exposures to private market assets are less than 50% of the Fund’s NAV.\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u64.8910\"},{\"quote\":\"Except for listed closed-ended alternative asset funds (LAFs).\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u63.8691\"},{\"quote\":\"In assessing whether the complex product designation is warranted, the SFC will adopt a holistic approach taking into account the specific circumstances of the case.\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u29.4630\"},{\"quote\":\"A Fund classified as a complex product will be subject to the SFC’s prevailing requirements for the sale of complex products including but not limited to ensuring the suitability of the Fund for its investors irrespective of whether solicitation or recommendation is involved.\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u32.4805\"},{\"quote\":\"Fund managers are encouraged to consult the SFC at the earliest opportunity if they are in doubt regarding complex product classification of their Funds.\",\"unit_id\":\"d4148dd852cee.u49.6955\"}],\"distinction\":\"The answered question is whether an in-scope Fund satisfies a ground requiring complex-product treatment for distribution. This is a condition predicate, not a compliance, prohibition, licence-possession, risk-rating or complete sales-permission finding. Mandatory threshold classification is distinct from discretionary designation; exclusion from this circular is not non-complex status; missing evidence is not a negative finding.\",\"family\":\"modality\",\"formalization\":{\"facts\":[{\"meaning\":\"The fund is authorised by the SFC for offering to the public in Hong Kong at the assessment time.\",\"name\":\"sfc_public_fund\",\"requires_judgment\":false,\"source_unit_ids\":[\"d4148dd852cee.u4.564\"],\"type\":\"bool\",\"unit\":\"Boolean authorisation status\"},{\"meaning\":\"The fund is a listed closed-ended alternative asset fund covered by footnote 6.\",\"name\":\"is_laf\",\"requires_judgment\":true,\"source_unit_ids\":[\"d4148dd852cee.u63.8691\"],\"type\":\"bool\",\"unit\":\"Boolean fund-category membership\"},{\"meaning\":\"Total direct and indirect exposure to private credit and private equity is at least 50% of NAV on the applicable, unresolved measurement basis and date. Insufficient data or unresolved conventions leave this fact unknown.\",\"name\":\"aggregate_exposure_at_least_half_nav\",\"requires_judgment\":true,\"source_unit_ids\":[\"d4148dd852cee.u1.5\",\"d4148dd852cee.u21.3779\",\"d4148dd852cee.u59.7979\"],\"type\":\"bool\",\"unit\":\"Boolean comparison of aggregate exposure with 50% of NAV\"},{\"meaning\":\"An SFC case-specific complex-product designation under this circular is operative for the fund at the assessment time.\",\"name\":\"effective_sfc_designation\",\"requires_judgment\":true,\"source_unit_ids\":[\"d4148dd852cee.u21.3779\",\"d4148dd852cee.u29.4630\",\"d4148dd852cee.u64.8910\"],\"type\":\"bool\",\"unit\":\"Boolean operative designation status\"}],\"result\":\"(or aggregate_exposure_at_least_half_nav effective_sfc_designation)\",\"result_type\":\"bool\",\"scope\":\"(and sfc_public_fund (not is_laf))\"},\"local_id\":\"reading.complex_classification\",\"questions\":[\"Has either the threshold or an operative SFC designation been established, or does missing evidence leave the result unresolved?\",\"Do clarification or the missing referenced rules resolve measurement, timing or cessation of classification?\"],\"statement\":\"[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] The result answers whether an SFC-authorised Fund within this circular satisfies a ground requiring treatment as a complex product for distribution. True means aggregate direct and indirect private-market exposure reaches at least 50% of NAV, including exactly 50%, or an operative SFC case-specific designation exists. False means both grounds are established absent at the relevant time; it does not establish non-complexity under every applicable regime. If neither ground is established and evidence is incomplete, the result is unknown. Below 50%, the SFC may designate holistically, considering aggregate exposure, strategy, portfolio composition, liquidity or risk profile, asset characteristics including CLO tranches and ratings and SRT structures and underlying assets, and home-regulator distribution conditions; these factors are non-exhaustive and do not automatically designate. LAFs fall outside this circular and require their separate regime. Private-market exposure routes are illustrative and updateable. The separate 15% direct-investment limit does not replace the 50% classification threshold. Classification brings prevailing complex-product sales requirements, including suitability regardless of solicitation or recommendation, and managers should select knowledgeable distributors. Existing-fund managers are expected to review, update documents as soon as practicable and communicate with distributors. No commencement, transition, measurement, reassessment or declassification rule is supplied; referenced rules and fund-specific evidence remain missing.\",\"subject\":\"Complex-product classification grounds for SFC-authorised funds under the retained circular\"}]}"}}
